id: warriors-pride
name: Warrior’s Pride
order: 3
category: mind
importance: secondary
# (2) "Ignore ... the effects of the Impaired and Fatigued Combat Conditions" while in the Superior State: still had, not
# felt (registry.mjs conditionPrograms).
ignoresConditions: impaired, fatigued
ignoresConditionsWhile: superior
description: >
  A proud race of warriors, Saiyans often hold their reputation above all else, believing themselves superior to all others in the heat of battle.
text: >
  Warrior’s Pride (Mind): A proud race of warriors, Saiyans often hold their reputation above all else, believing themselves superior to all others in the heat of battle.
  (1)-[Passive]: Apply your Racial Saving Throw Bonus to Cognitive as well as Corporeal.
  (2)-[Passive]: While you are in the Superior State, ignore any Health Threshold Penalties and the effects of the Impaired and Fatigued Combat Conditions.
  (3)-[Triggered/Raging, Triggered/Power, 1/Encounter]: Enter the Superior State until the end of your next turn.
  (4)-[Triggered/Start of Combat Encounter]: Gain a stack of Battle Born.

---

# (1) Cognitive as well: 1(T) on it and its Critical Target 1 lower, as the race's own Saving Throw has.
[passive]
allow save.racial.cognitive;

# (2) In the Superior State, no Health Threshold Penalties - and Impaired and Fatigued not felt (the header above).
[passive]
if (inState("superior")) {
    threshold.penalty = 0;
}

# (3) On entering the Raging State, or on the Power Up Maneuver - asked in a window there and then - Superior until the
# end of your next turn. Both are the one effect: once per Encounter between them.
[triggered/state/raging, 1/encounter, effect 3]
enterState(superior, 1, next-turn);

[triggered/power, 1/encounter, effect 3]
enterState(superior, 1, next-turn);

# (4) The Combat Encounter beginning: a stack of Battle Born (Born for Battle's), put where you say.
[triggered/start-of-encounter, effect 4]
gainOneOf(battlebornstrike, battleborndodge, battlebornwound);
